ot going to know the answer to  that question the manager is however  going to know he potentially has a  public relations nightmare on their  hands because nobody wants to be  associated with the production of  weapons designed to violate the  fundamental principles of international  humanitarian law something you can  everybody can do this and it's pretty  straightforward and there's a lot of  examples on our website of letters you  can send if you don't want to just send  them a quickie quickie message we also  found some great success with this and a  couple of people saw an article and  newspaper in Sweden and started a little  Facebook like they started asking  questions on Facebook of their bank that  bank now has a pretty good policy on  doesn't invest in any nuclear weapon  producers this Fed bank because they've  picked out because the public relations  relations nightmare so that's something  if you probably have a lot of you have  pension funds you can ask the same  questions of your pension funds and I  hope you have insurance because  insurance is important we can ask the  same questions for your insurance agents  are you sure insurance companies all of  these are potential investors in the  nuclear weapon production complex and  you can find out you know if they are  investing using our report or you can  just ask them directly so that's quite  quite cool and they'll answer you which  is nice it's nice to see and nice to see  something that's that's very winnable in  this but when you personally do now if  you want to work together with other  people because that's always very good  there's ways to take this issue around  divestment and take it to the city level  here in Cambridge there was a great  example of this as announced last year  and mayor Simmons referred to it this  morning there is a resolution passed in  the City Council to make sure that the  that the city pension council pension  fund is not invested in nuclear weapon  producers since t